1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,141
This week I changed what I'm entering.

2
00:00:03,191 --> 00:00:06,333
Confide stays where it was submitted first;

3
00:00:06,383 --> 00:00:13,627
for this fair I moved to the Tempo track, where my Reth and Revm work fits.

4
00:00:13,677 --> 00:00:15,451
The product is Sworn.

5
00:00:15,501 --> 00:00:21,826
On MPP, if a paid answer is wrong, a refund is the server's choice.

6
00:00:21,876 --> 00:00:26,835
Sworn makes the server reserve its own bond behind each answer.

7
00:00:26,885 --> 00:00:32,299
Here a server says the payment lands; Tempo's receive policy diverts it.

8
00:00:32,349 --> 00:00:36,397
A zero-knowledge proof of Tempo's own EVM catches it,

9
00:00:36,447 --> 00:00:40,951
and the bond pays the agent — this transaction, on Moderato.

10
00:00:41,001 --> 00:00:49,179
What I learned: our first full run said "blocked" but the transfer had simply run out of gas

11
00:00:49,229 --> 00:00:52,379
— Tempo prices storage about eleven times Ethereum.

12
00:00:52,429 --> 00:00:54,207
The test caught it.

13
00:00:54,257 --> 00:00:56,950
Next: the demo and the submission.
